// Quazi self-host compiler — design scaffold, NOT implementation.
// Component: syntax
// File: expressions.qz
// Responsibility: Expression syntax.
// Package boundary: Quazi-specific lexical and syntactic frontend; independent of QZI and machine backends.
// TODO(P0/P1): implement existing bootstrap behavior with clean interfaces.
// Do not introduce new language features before bootstrap parity.
// Split boundary: this file remains the coordinator for its responsibility;
// implementation details belong to the adjacent modules listed below.
//   expression/precedence.qz: Expression operator precedence and associativity parsing; binary/range/assignment operator chains.
//   expression/postfix.qz: Postfix parsing for calls, indexing, field/method access and explicit type arguments.
//   expression/primary.qz: Primary expressions: literals, names, parenthesized expressions, constructors and closures.
//   expression/patterns.qz: Patterns and match-arm grammar used by match expressions; no semantic exhaustiveness checks.
